<h3>What Drives Wallpaper Cost?</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Material substrate:</strong> PVC foam is cheapest; silk and natural fibre are most expensive</li>
  <li><strong>Printing technology:</strong> Digital HD printing adds ₹20–₹80/sq ft over plain patterns</li>
  <li><strong>Thickness &amp; layers:</strong> Multi-layer vinyl with foam backing commands a 30–50% premium</li>
  <li><strong>Brand positioning:</strong> MNC brands (Marshalls, D'Decor) cost 25–40% more than domestic manufacturers</li>
  <li><strong>Imported vs. domestic:</strong> European and Korean imports carry 18–35% import duties plus GST</li>
  <li><strong>Texture complexity:</strong> Embossed and 3D textures require specialised tooling — adds ₹30–₹100/sq ft</li>
  <li><strong>Surface preparation:</strong> Rough or damp walls requiring extensive putty work add ₹800–₹2,500 to project cost</li>
  <li><strong>Installation in Tier 1 cities:</strong> Labour in Mumbai/Delhi/Bangalore runs 20–30% higher than Tier 2</li>
</ul>
