<h2>Section 06 Room-Wise Wallpaper Selection Guide</h2>
<p>The best wallpaper for each room is determined by three factors: <strong>traffic level, humidity exposure, and desired mood.</strong> Here are our recommendations:</p>
<p>Living Room</p>
<p>Non-Woven or Vinyl, Feature Wall</p>
<p>Use bold patterns on one accent wall. Matte or satin finish for ambient lighting. Avoid high-gloss on large surfaces — it creates glare.</p>
<p>Bedroom</p>
<p>Fabric-Look or Soft Vinyl, Headboard Wall</p>
<p>Soft textures and muted colours for restful sleep. Install on the headboard wall only — full-room wallpaper can feel overwhelming.</p>
<p>Kids Room</p>
<p>Vinyl (Washable), Custom Mural</p>
<p>Scrubbable vinyl handles crayon marks and food splashes. Custom cartoon/theme murals at ₹100–₹200/sq ft are surprisingly affordable.</p>
<p>Home Office / Study</p>
<p>Textured Neutral or Wood-Look</p>
<p>Low-stimulation textures improve focus. A wood-look or concrete-finish wallpaper on one wall signals professional character on video calls.</p>
<p>TV Unit Wall</p>
<p>3D or Stone Texture Wallpaper</p>
<p>The TV unit wall is India's most popular single-wall application. 3D brick, stone, or wood panel wallpapers at ₹120–₹350/sq ft transform the entire room's focal point.</p>
<p>Dining Room</p>
<p>Metallic or Grasscloth Accent</p>
<p>Dining rooms see low traffic and no moisture. Use bolder choices — metallic foil, grasscloth, or deep botanical prints. These spaces can handle a luxury wallpaper investment.</p>
<p>Foyer / Entrance</p>
<p>Durable Vinyl, Bold Pattern</p>
<p>High traffic and the first impression of your home. Choose a durable washable vinyl with a statement pattern. Dark colours in small entrance foyers create drama without feeling claustrophobic.</p>
<p>Kitchen</p>
<p>Waterproof Vinyl (Backsplash Area)</p>
<p>Standard wallpaper cannot survive near stovetops or sinks. Use only oil-and-waterproof vinyl, limited to walls away from direct heat and steam. Behind stoves — always use tiles instead.</p>
<div class="callout callout--warn"><span class="callout__title">Watch out</span>⚠️<br><br><strong>Avoid Wallpaper in Bathrooms (Most Cases)</strong><br><br>Standard wallpaper — including most vinyl — is not suitable for full bathroom application in India due to steam and water splashes. Waterproof ceramic or porcelain tiles remain the correct choice. Exception: powder rooms (no shower/bath) can use high-quality vinyl on walls above the tile line.</div>
