    <tr><th>Problem</th><th>Cause</th><th>Solution</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><strong>Peeling at edges</strong></td><td>High humidity, poor adhesive</td><td>Waterproof adhesive + edge sealer</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Mould under wallpaper</strong></td><td>Seepage or condensation on cold walls</td><td>Anti-mould primer + fix seepage source</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Bubbling in monsoon</strong></td><td>Wall moisture expanding behind paper</td><td>Fully dry wall before install; use non-woven</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Colour fading (south-facing walls)</strong></td><td>UV exposure through windows</td><td>UV-resistant vinyl; use UV-blocking window film</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Adhesive failure in heat</strong></td><td>High-VOC adhesives degrade above 40°C</td><td>Use heat-stable starch or acrylic adhesive</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>
<h2>Section 12 Interior vs. Exterior Wallpapers</h2>
<p>The vast majority of wallpapers sold in India — and globally — are designed exclusively for interior use. Here is why and what the exterior market looks like:</p>
<h3>Interior Wallpaper (Standard)</h3>
<p>All the types discussed above are interior products. They are not engineered to withstand direct rain, UV radiation, temperature extremes, or biological growth from outdoor exposure. Installing a standard interior wallpaper on an exterior-facing wall (even inside a room) near windows or on uninsulated external walls accelerates degradation significantly.</p>
<h3>Exterior Wallpaper / Façade Cladding</h3>
<p>A small category of UV-stabilised, waterproof vinyl wraps and weather-resistant textured panels exist for exterior commercial applications — typically shopping centres, retail façades, and commercial buildings. These are not wallpaper in the traditional sense but large-format vinyl graphics and architectural films. Cost: ₹300–₹800/sq ft installed. Lifespan with UV-laminate: 5–8 years outdoors.</p>
<h2>Section 13 Custom Wallpaper Guide</h2>
<p>Custom wallpaper — printing any image at wall-scale — has become genuinely mainstream in India since 2022, driven by the availability of wide-format UV and latex printers. Here's everything you need to know:</p>
<h3>What Custom Wallpaper Can Do</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Family photograph murals:</strong> A family portrait printed at 8×4 ft on a bedroom wall — ₹5,000–₹15,000 total</li>
  <li><strong>Kids themed rooms:</strong> Cartoon characters, outer space, underwater worlds, sports themes — all fully custom at ₹100–₹200/sq ft</li>
  <li><strong>Landscape murals:</strong> Forest, mountain, ocean, cityscape printed at photographic resolution — the most popular category</li>
  <li><strong>Office branding walls:</strong> Company logo, values, team photography, product murals — a growing B2B market</li>
  <li><strong>Religious and spiritual artwork:</strong> Custom devotional murals, Tanjore-inspired digital prints, mandala backgrounds</li>
</ul>
<h3>Custom Wallpaper Cost (2026)</h3>
<p>Custom printing on standard vinyl: <strong>₹100–₹200/sq ft.</strong> Premium non-woven substrate: <strong>₹180–₹350/sq ft.</strong> Canvas-textured substrate: <strong>₹250–₹500/sq ft.</strong> Minimum order is typically 20–30 sq ft. Lead time: 3–7 business days.</p>
<h3>Custom Wallpaper Selection Checklist</h3>
<ul>
  <li>Image resolution minimum 150 DPI at final print size (300 DPI for close-viewing distance)</li>
  <li>Wall measurements taken precisely including doors, windows, sockets</li>
  <li>Image colours reviewed on a printed proof or physical swatch — never judge from a screen alone</li>
  <li>Theme chosen for long-term relevance — avoid trend-dependent choices for permanent walls</li>
  <li>Lighting conditions considered — dark images on north-facing walls absorb available light</li>
  <li>Furniture colours coordinated with wallpaper palette before ordering</li>
  <li>Printing material selected (vinyl for humid rooms; non-woven for dry rooms, easier removal)</li>
  <li>Seam plan reviewed — where will vertical seams fall relative to focal points?</li>
  <li>UV-laminate specified if wall receives direct sunlight</li>
  <li>Installation quoted as part of order — most custom vendors offer package pricing</li>
</ul>
<h2>Section 15 Wallpaper Installation Process</h2>
<p>Professional installation is the difference between a 2-year wallpaper and a 12-year wallpaper — even with identical materials. Here is the correct process:</p>
<p>1</p>
<p><strong>Site Measurement &amp; Planning</strong></p>
<p>Measure wall height and width precisely. Add 5cm on each side for trimming. Calculate total sq ft and add 10–15% for pattern matching waste.</p>
<p>2</p>
<p><strong>Surface Inspection</strong></p>
<p>Check for cracks, loose plaster, seepage, mould, or efflorescence. All issues must be resolved before any further steps — wallpaper does not hide structural problems.</p>
<p>3</p>
<p><strong>Putty &amp; Sanding</strong></p>
<p>Apply white cement putty (2 coats) to fill all imperfections. Sand smooth to a flat, even surface. Allow 24 hours drying per coat. This is the step most budget contractors skip — and it's the most important.</p>
<p>4</p>
<p><strong>Primer Application</strong></p>
<p>Apply a PVA-based or acrylic wall primer. For high-humidity walls, use anti-mould primer. Primer seals the surface, reduces absorption, and improves adhesive bond. Allow 4–6 hours to dry.</p>
<p>5</p>
<p><strong>Adhesive Preparation</strong></p>
<p>Mix adhesive per manufacturer instructions — either powder-to-water ratio for starch adhesives or ready-mix vinyl adhesive straight from container. Do not use Fevicol or white glue — they create bubble hotspots.</p>
<p>6</p>
<p><strong>Wallpaper Cutting &amp; Pattern Matching</strong></p>
<p>Cut panels 5–10cm longer than wall height. For patterned wallpaper, lay out all panels before pasting to confirm pattern repeat matching across seams.</p>
<p>7</p>
<p><strong>Pasting &amp; Hanging</strong></p>
<p>For paste-the-wall method: apply adhesive to wall, hang panel, smooth from centre outward. For paste-the-paper: apply adhesive to panel back, allow to soak 3–5 minutes, then hang. Use a plumb line for the first panel — every subsequent panel follows from it.</p>
<p>8</p>
<p><strong>Bubble Removal &amp; Seam Pressing</strong></p>
<p>Use a smoothing brush or plastic squeegee to work out air bubbles from centre to edges. Press seams firmly with a seam roller. Do not leave bubbles to "dry out" — they don't.</p>
<p>9</p>
<p><strong>Edge Trimming &amp; Finishing</strong></p>
<p>Use a straight-edge metal ruler and sharp craft knife to trim along skirting boards, ceiling, and door/window frames. A blunt blade tears; replace blade every 3–4 cuts.</p>
<p>10</p>
<p><strong>Final Inspection &amp; Drying</strong></p>
<p>Inspect every seam, edge, and bubble under raking light (torch held sideways). Allow 24–48 hours to dry with room well-ventilated before pushing furniture back against the wall.</p>
